Theorem CN-5: Unique plus Dead preserves reusable shape

  Preconditions:
    - s.uniqueness = Unique
    - s.consumption = Dead (implies s.cardinality = Absent via CN-1)
    - s.shape in {ReusableStruct, ReusableEnum, CollectionBuffer, ContextHole}

  Soundness property:
    No CN rule collapses ReusableCtor on Unique plus Dead inputs.

  Proof obligation:
    Implicit-invariant absence check. Compose canonicalize over 4 reusable
    Shape variants with (Unique, Dead, Absent): CN-3 does NOT fire
    (uniqueness =/= Shared), CN-1 already at fixpoint (Dead+Absent).
    Verify shape preserved in all 4 cases.

    Engines dispatched:
      case_analysis (4-shape absence-check per
        section_03::verify_cn5_unique_dead_preserves_shape)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_03 case_analysis engine discharges CN-5 via 4-shape absence check on Unique+Dead state
